--- uber refresh / authority lines in away-quiet-supervision at HEAD:
21:- A message beginning `/afk` or `/uberafk` refreshes away mode; a message beginning `/quiet` or `/uberquiet` refreshes quiet mode.
22:- Any other unmarked message means the captain returned in away mode (load `/afk`, run the return owner, and do not process that message as ordinary work until its durable catch-up gate clears), or, in quiet mode, is simply answered as ordinary work with the flag and daemon left untouched until an explicit `/quiet off` or `/uberquiet off`.
23:- Away and quiet mode never create approval authority beyond the recorded words and standing rules; the guarded scripts and `ask-user-authority` policy still apply.
